# The object editor (olc.c's oedit and do_oedit, olc_act.c's oedit_*, show_obj_values and set_obj_values), with
# Planner (security 9) in Midgaard, and Delver (security 0). The string editor's "@" is sent as "x", a backspace,
# "@" (see redit.scn).
# - oedit with no vnum, a bad one, create's refusals; edit object 3011 (bread); show, commands, version
# - name, short (lower-cased first letter), long (upper-cased), weight, cost, level, material, condition, extra,
#   wear and type, with their refusals
# - addaffect and addapply with each refusal (addapply checks the bits before the modifier, and "object" names
#   its bits from the apply locations), then delaffect by number
# - extra descriptions: add, edit, format, delete, and keywords not found
# - v0-v4 on food (a value it doesn't have shows its help), then a new object (3007) through every item type:
#   light, wand, staff, portal, furniture, scroll, potion, pill, armor, weapon, container (key refusals), drink,
#   fountain, money, and trash (no values at all)
# - asave changed saves Midgaard; the room editor's oshow; after a save, creating an object, and setting a
#   value on trash (which has none), each mark the area changed again
# - Delver can't edit or create
@connect b
Planner
smoke123
@return
@return
scroll 0
goto 3001
force hassan oedit 3011
oedit
oedit 99999
oedit create
oedit create 99999
oedit create 3011
edit object 3011
@return
